  "slug": "hearings-09-mechanism",
  "title": "Closing arguments — the pieces of linking an argument to the evidence it invokes, and their relationships",
  "titleEs": "Conclusiones de las partes — Mecanismo o relación explicada",
  "category": "hearings",
  "categoryName": "Audiencias y desarrollo del juicio",
  "motif": "Conclusiones de las partes",
  "treatment": "mechanism",
  "family": "spatial-mechanism",
  "description": "An exploded view of a generic hearing room: the two argument cards leave the board through the top wall to a band above the room, card A to one side and card B, mirrored, to the other, and the numbered exhibits lift off the evidence table to a row between them; the parties stay at their identical lecterns. Each piece is labelled on the plan. Only the supplied relationships are drawn, with their kind captioned on the plan (a party puts its card forward; each card is linked to every exhibit it invokes, as supplied); a relationship and its mirror on the other side are drawn together. A tracer follows the supplied traversal and a second one its mirror, at the same time; the element reached enlarges, the focus most. Both cards get the same neutral frame. Illustrative; nothing is proved, weighed or decided and no side is preferred.",
